{%- comment -%}
  A cart line's price, with what it was struck through and what it saves.

  The "was" price comes from whichever source applies to the line, because
  Shopify reports no discount on a subscription: a selling plan sets the line's
  own price, so original_line_price equals final_line_price and total_discount
  is zero. The plan's allocation carries compare_at_price instead.

  Whichever is highest of: the plan's compare-at, the variant's compare-at,
  and original_line_price if a cart discount has beaten both. Highest rather
  than first-that-answers, because a subscription line carries both compare-ats
  and the plan's own is only the one-time price - struck against that, a
  subscription that takes 30% off the full price reads as saving the difference
  from the sale price instead. sections/main-product.liquid strikes the
  subscribe price against the same basis.

  Nothing renders but the price when there is no saving to show, so a
  full-price line stays quiet rather than reading "Save $0".

  Accepts: item (a cart line item).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign was_unit = 0 -%}
{%- if item.selling_plan_allocation.compare_at_price > was_unit -%}
  {%- assign was_unit = item.selling_plan_allocation.compare_at_price -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if item.variant.compare_at_price > was_unit -%}
  {%- assign was_unit = item.variant.compare_at_price -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%} Nothing to strike through if the line is already at or above it. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if was_unit <= item.final_price -%}
  {%- assign was_unit = 0 -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- assign was_line = was_unit | times: item.quantity -%}
{%- if item.original_line_price > was_line -%}
  {%- assign was_line = item.original_line_price -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign saved = was_line | minus: item.final_line_price -%}

{%- if saved > 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%} The pair is wrapped so that putting them side by side stays one box as far as the layout is concerned: loose, the column has to be wide enough for both plus the saving, which is what squeezed the title beside it. {%- endcomment -%}
  <span class="cart-line-prices">
    <s class="cart-line-was">{{ was_line | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</s>
    <span class="cart-line-now">{{ item.final_line_price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
  </span>
  <span class="cart-line-save">(Save {{ saved | money_without_trailing_zeros }})</span>
{%- else -%}
  <span class="cart-line-now">{{ item.final_line_price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
